# Embedded Codex Agent Instructions

## Authority And Execution

- Complete the bootstrap in root `AGENTS.md`; its critical safety tripwires remain binding. Within this file, paths are relative to `codex/` unless explicitly repository-rooted.
- Resolve conflicts by instruction priority: system/developer and active runtime constraints, then explicit user instructions, then repository instructions. Within repository instructions, use the designated canonical policy for the subject; role files and handoff text cannot override it. Apply compatible additional safety conditions together, rather than reviving conflicting guidance because it is stricter.
- Continue authorized work through completion using reasonable assumptions for routine choices. Same-task approval persists within its scope under `docs/policies/approvals.md`. If an instruction requires stopping, cite its exact file and clause, explain the concrete blocker, and continue independent authorized work where possible.
- Prefer the permission profile in `docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md`. Report a more restrictive runtime before broad project/MCP work; instructions cannot change runtime permissions or authorize bypasses. Broad access does not authorize credentials, secrets, account, remote, destructive-history, unrelated-work, or system-security changes.
- Model choice, same-agent execution, delegation, independent review, verification tiers, evidence reuse, and paid routes are governed by `docs/policies/cost-control.md`; consult it when those decisions arise.
- Pre-deduplication source: `snapshots/20260906-before-bootstrap-dedup/codex-AGENTS.md` (historical, immutable).
- Pre-alignment source: `snapshots/20260908-astra-instruction-alignment/codex/AGENTS.md` (historical, immutable).

## Work Visibility

- Report in Korean; preserve identifiers, paths, commands, APIs, exact errors, and literals where translation reduces accuracy.
- Before tool-assisted work, briefly state the objective. For a short read-only task, one sentence is sufficient; name a role only when it helps explain responsibility. Before mutation, state the affected target, intended change, and purpose; include concrete risk or approval context when applicable.
- During longer work, report concise milestones, blockers, evidence, and next safe actions rather than per-command chatter. Do not expose secrets, credentials, large logs, or low-signal output.
- Honor silence or status-only requests except required safety/approval/destructive/external-state notices. Role guidance may strengthen these duties within instruction priority.

## Text Encoding Safety

- Unreal authoring names must use English: Blueprint variables, material parameters, and equivalent editor controls must have English identifiers, display/friendly names, and categories. Do not add Korean names through `DisplayName` or `friendly_name`. Write descriptive Korean explanations only in tooltips. When modifying these controls, check their visible names as well as their underlying identifiers before saving.

- Preserve UTF-8, BOM, and line-ending choices defined by `.editorconfig` at the repository root. Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads require `Get-Content -Encoding UTF8`.
- Use `apply_patch` for normal edits. Scripted writes require an explicit UTF-8 encoder; use `System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)` for no BOM rather than PowerShell 5.1 `Set-Content -Encoding UTF8`.
- If output is garbled, re-read with explicit UTF-8 and verify original bytes or `git diff` before editing.
- For a full encoding audit, run `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File codex/scripts/check-text-encoding.ps1 -AllTracked` from the repository root. The versioned pre-commit hook checks staged text only in clones configured with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.

## Conditional Reading Index

Read only matching entries. Component rows are mutually conditional; combine them only for work genuinely spanning those components.

| Decision or task | Canonical starting source |
| --- | --- |
| Workspace, engine, executable, or multi-PC paths | `docs/policies/workspace-portability.md` |
| Runtime/session/ACL permissions | `docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md` |
| Git, dirty/concurrent work, repository boundaries | `docs/policies/git-repositories.md`; `docs/policies/approvals.md` when approval scope matters |
| Durable memory or instruction thinning | `docs/policies/documentation-memory.md` |
| Model/agent choice, verification cadence, paid API routes | `docs/policies/cost-control.md` |
| Mutation/retry, C++, dependency, lifecycle, encoding, or destructive risk | `docs/policies/safety-matrix.md`, then every matching canonical source before the governed action |
| Component inspection, implementation, or verification | `docs/workflows/component-reading-router.md`, matching rows only |
| Named role | Matching file in `agents/`; planning: `agents/ieta.md`; MCP implementation: `agents/tivret-mcp.md` |
| RPC transport/retry reliability | `docs/workflows/mcp-rpc-verification-first.md` |
| Smoke validation | `agents/tivret-mcp.md` and `docs/workflows/mcp-smoke-test-protocol.md` |
| Upstream update, including 최신 업데이트 / 업데이트 받아줘 / 원본 pull / upstream 최신 / chongdashu 최신 | `agents/mcp-upstream-manager.md` and `docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md` |
| Release verification | `agents/mcp-release-verifier.md` and project binding verification entry point |
| Unreal C++ review | `agents/unreal-cpp-reviewer.md` and `docs/workflows/unreal-cpp-review.md` |
| Repository-owned Codex skills | Applicable `SKILL.md` under `skills/` |
| Claude adapter | `integrations/claude-code/README.md`; keep Claude wrappers outside Codex `skills/` |
| New section, cross-repository orchestration, rule promotion | Matching workflow under `docs/workflows/` |
| Instruction or routing evaluation | `docs/workflows/agent-instruction-evaluation.md` |

## Shared Editor And Memory

- Treat the effective editor bridge endpoint as shared. Before launch, close, map changes, dirty prompts, or `QUIT_EDITOR`, inspect process/log context and coordinate with other users/agents. Use the safety matrix for lifecycle rules; for multi-asset or multi-step bridge work also read repository-root `Docs/Tools/batch_tools.md`.
- Update durable documentation only within approved scope and use Git-tracked documents as canonical memory. Follow `docs/policies/documentation-memory.md` for placement and immutable snapshots before thinning instructions. Git authorization remains governed by the Git/approval policies.
- Do not read external project bindings or resolve external repositories unless the user explicitly names that scope.
